    }
  ],
  "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
  "rights": {
    "status": "public_domain",
    "architects": [],
    "built": 1350,
    "note": "Medieval walls with no known architect: begun at the end of the 11th century (traditionally 1090, after the repopulation under Raymond of Burgundy), built mostly in the 12th century (the cathedral apse, the cimorro, was built into the east wall c. 1160–1180) and reinforced in the 14th century; 'built' = the end of those medieval works (approximate). Restorations of the 19th–20th centuries kept the medieval design."
  },
